Experiment patch, not a proposed fix yet. Applies to rocm-systems at tag hip-version_10.1.62330
(the wheel pin). Adds the CopyToKernel acquire on the main engine after an SDMA buffer copy,
mirroring what the CP DMA branch already emits at the end of Resource::partialMemCopyTo.
Rebuild amdhip64_7.dll with PDB, then run six fresh starts, workaround off.

Apply from the rocm-systems checkout root:  git apply --check clr-sdma-acquire.patch

--- a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/pal/palresource.cpp
+++ b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/pal/palresource.cpp
@@ -1690,6 +1690,14 @@ bool Resource::partialMemCopyTo(VirtualGPU& gpu, const amd::Coord3D& srcOrigin,
   // Restore the original engine
   gpu.engineID_ = activeEngineID;

+  if (!cp_dma && (activeEngineID == MainEngine)) {
+    // EXPERIMENT: the SDMA branch has no CopyToKernel acquire, unlike the CP DMA branch above.
+    // The next compute submit only does a CPU-side WaitForIdleSdma(), which orders the work but
+    // does not invalidate the compute caches for the range SDMA just wrote. Emit the same acquire
+    // on the main engine so the consumer kernel cannot read stale lines.
+    gpu.addBarrier(RgpSqqtBarrierReason::MemDependency, BarrierType::CopyToKernel);
+  }
+
   return true;
 }

